nd no configuration, it sets up all the framebuffers and a good default mode and then displays them on screen. The actual application can pull the framebuffers out of the app to do rendering using EGL or mapping to user space for CPU rendering.  The app class is highly coupled to other classes within bsdrm because it is meant to integrate many features of the library for ease of use. It may not be possible to do your drm-test using bs_app, in which case you should probably just skip using it.  BUG=None TEST=drm-tests still builds  Change-Id: I5d3a9ca95da8b1018bb0cb0d1fc8f064f71b8d9f Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/327674 Commit-Ready: Zach Reizner &lt;zachr@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Zach Reizner &lt;zachr@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Haixia Shi &lt;hshi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="327674" owner_email="zachr@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/drm-tests" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/drm-tests" ref="refs/changes/74/327674/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I8737a28e85ce85a233faca82824cb7883a6d9e16" commit="3b8b854ec32bcef85307b686883b903cdb45d0ff" commit_message="Update master-toolchain-release buildslave_type.  As previously requested, this CL adds buildslave_type=constants.GCE_WIMPY_BUILD_SLAVE_TYPE to the master-toolchain-release buildbot.  This is part of the conversion of toolchain-llvm to a master-slave configuration.  BUG=None TEST=Ran unittests; all passed.  Change-Id: I8737a28e85ce85a233faca82824cb7883a6d9e16 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/327686 Commit-Ready: Caroline Tice &lt;cmtice@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Caroline Tice &lt;cmtice@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Caroline Tice &lt;cmtice@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="327686" owner_email="cmtice@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://c